meta {
  name: Sign Up
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-up/email
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Origin: {{clientUrl}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Test User",
    "email": "you@example.com",
    "password": "password123"
  }
}

docs {
  Better Auth serves this, it is not hand written.

  requireEmailVerification is on, so the account is created but cannot sign in
  until the emailed link is opened. The verification mail is sent automatically.

  In development the verification URL is also printed to the API server log, which
  is the practical way to get the token without leaving the terminal.
}
